  "details": "<p>The\u00a0Via *Quinctia is included on map 41 of the\u00a0<em>Barrington Atlas </em>(41 D2). It is also cross-referenced\u00a0<span>on map 42 A1 of the\u00a0</span><em>Barrington Atlas\u00a0</em>under the \"roads\" category.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A road named Via *Quinctia linked Florentia (Firenze) to Pisae (Pisa) in northern Etruria. Its construction is ascribed to the consul Titus Quinctius Flamininus starting in 123 BCE.",
